      "output_preview": "## Phase 1 \u2014 API Schemas: Complete \u2705\n\n### What was accomplished\n\nCreated the `team-test/api/` package with two files:\n\n#### `team-test/api/__init__.py`\nSimple package marker with a docstring describing the API package.\n\n#### `team-test/api/schemas.py`\nFull Pydantic v2 request/response schema module with 9 classes:\n\n**User schemas:**\n- `UserBase` \u2014 shared fields: `username` (3\u201350 chars), `email` (EmailStr), `full_name` (optional, \u2264100 chars), `is_active` (default True)\n- `UserCreate(UserBase)` \u2014 adds `password` (plain-text, min 6 chars) for `POST /users/`\n- `UserUpdate` \u2014 all-optional PATCH body: `full_name`, `is_active`, `password`\n- `UserResponse(UserBase)` \u2014 adds `id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`; `model_config = ConfigDict(from_attributes=True)` for ORM\u2192Pydantic; **never exposes `hashed_password`**\n\n**Project schemas:**\n- `ProjectBase` \u2014 shared fields: `name` (1\u2013100 chars), `description` (optional), `is_active` (default True)\n- `ProjectCreate(ProjectBase)` \u2014 adds `owner_id` (must reference existing User) for `POST /projects/`\n- `ProjectUpdate` \u2014 all-optional PATCH body: `name`, `description`, `is_active`\n- `ProjectResponse(ProjectBase)` \u2014 adds `id`, `owner_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`; `from_attributes=True`\n\n**Generic wrapper:**\n- `MessageResponse` \u2014 `{\"message\": \"...\"}` for DELETE confirmations etc.\n\n### Verification\n- `python -m py_compile` \u2014 syntax clean \u2705\n- 12 live validation checks executed and all passed \u2705:\n  - Happy-path construction for all schema types\n  - `UserCreate` rejects username < 3 chars, password < 6 chars, invalid email\n  - `ProjectCreate` rejects empty name\n  - `UserUpdate` / `ProjectUpdate` accept fully-empty bodies (all fields optional)\n  - `UserResponse.model_validate(orm_instance)` works via `from_attributes=True`\n  - `ProjectResponse.model_validate(orm_instance)` works via `from_attributes=True`\n  - `hashed_password` confirmed absent from `UserResponse.model_dump()`",
